Hey,

I'm doing the following using dplyr and it works great:
test1 <- raw_data_rt %>%
 group_by(subject) %>%
 summarise(n = mean(rt[abs(z_score) < 1])) %>%
 dcast(subject ~ "t1rt", value.var = "n", fun = mean).

> head(test1)
  subject      t1rt
1      99  999.3180
2    5203  929.3739
3    5205 1124.2645
4    5306  978.6618
5    5307 1120.1499
6    5308 1019.4909

The thing is that now I want to incorporate this within a function such that the name of the column to group_by is not always subject. One of my function arguments is id which is the name of the columns to group_by. However, if instead of subject I write raw_data_rt[[id]] I get NAs in thet1rt column:

          test1 <- raw_data_rt %>%
            group_by(raw_data_rt[[id]]) %>%
            summarise(n = mean(rt[abs(z_score) < 1])) %>%
            dcast(raw_data_rt[[id]] ~ "t1rt", value.var = "n", fun = mean)

> head(test1)
  raw_data_rt[[id]] t1rt
1                99   NA
2              5203   NA
3              5205   NA
4              5306   NA
5              5307   NA
6              5308   NA

 What can I do to solve this?

Any help will be greatly appreciated

Ayala

