Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I would say that you should maybe use standard evaluation. The input of standard evaluation could be the name of that column in quotes.

So group_by_() instead of group_by().
id = "something"

test1 <- raw_data_rt %>%

 group_by_(id) %>%

 summarise(n = mean(rt[abs(z_score) < 1])) %>%
 dcast(subject ~ "t1rt", value.var = "n", fun = mean)

See:

vignette("nse")

I don't know if you can mix NSE and SE so this may not work, but you didn't provide a dataset to play with either and I'm feeling lazy today.

HTH,

B

